  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Som tum serves 2 and takes about 15 minutes. The salad is traditionally made with shredded green papaya, which has no slug in this library, so use shredded beansprouts and a firm shredded vegetable such as green cabbage or courgette to give the correct texture. The dressing is the same: lime, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "fish sauce",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "fish-sauce"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "palm sugar",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "palm-sugar"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", and chilli."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work the dressing in the mortar before adding the vegetables. Pound the chilli and garlic first, then add the wet ingredients and taste before the salad goes in."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
